  "stem": "A ball is dropped from a height of 512 centimeters. After each bounce, it rises to \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\) of the height from which it last fell. What is the height, in centimeters, that the ball reaches after its third bounce?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "216"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "The height after \\(n\\) bounces is \\(H(n) = 512\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^{n}\\).",
    "\\(H(3) = 512 \\cdot \\frac{27}{64} = 216\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "n = symbols('n')\nH = Lambda(n, 512*Rational(3, 4)**n)\nassert H(3) == 216\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == [H(3)]",
